<p>My push to get ready for the Edmonds Art Fair continues. I'm focusing on smaller works so that I'll have more inventory at an affordable price point.</p>
<p>Painting at this scale is a lot of fun, but you have to come up with a constant stream of ideas to keep it going.</p>
<p>For these small works, I will usually do the designs for up to a dozen all at the same time. When I start to paint I can then get into an uninterrupted flow.</p>
